@world.calc.story core.world
    namespace=calc.story
    version=0.1.0
    legend=$legend.calc.story
    imports=world.core
    imports=world.lang.common
    imports=world.acts
    formalization=rules
    reader=yes
    language=en
    status=fixture
    title="Word problems"
    summary="solve word problems"
    doc="A general world, not a tab (kids plan, ADR-011, Q18 L1): a story of quantities that owners hold (Tom has 15 apples. He gives 12 to Ana. How many apples does Tom have?) is read by the library's storyState, sentence by sentence and across turns (the story is the world state). The library decides the owner (a name, a pronoun for the last owner, I, or a number as subject: One flies away), the amount (a number, a or an for one) and the item, refuses giving or losing more than is held with the reason, and answers how many an owner holds, all together, at first, how many more, who has the most. Nothing here lists names or things: the number words, pronouns and function words come from the language world (w.lang.en through src/lang/en.mjs), the verbs and their effects from k.actions' typed possession effects (K5: the phrase groups acts.possession.* of worlds/acts, generated in every form) and, for the verbs k.actions has no effect for yet, lang.common's phrase groups lang.story.*. Hand-built platform fixture, not produced by the C1 workflow."
